<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sweyn Haakonsson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1016</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sveinn Hákonarson, Svein Haakonsson</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sweyn Haakonsson was a Norwegian earl of Lade, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hakon-sigurdsson">Håkon Sigurdsson</a>. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-svolder">Battle of Svolder</a> in 1000 he and his brother Eric governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> for the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>. He was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olaf-ii-of-norway">Olaf Haraldsson</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nesjar">Battle of Nesjar</a> in 1016, fled to Sweden and died soon after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sweyn-haakonsson.jpg" alt="Sweyn Haakonsson" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tokle NordNordWest; derivative work by Ecelan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Norway_1000_AD-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
